    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nThe number pattern for predicate parameters uses an unescaped `.`, which matches any character, so parameters such as \"1a2\" and \"12x34\" are highlighted as numbers.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nMatch a literal dot. A single backslash escape does not survive query string parsing, so use a character class.",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-09T07:27:29Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Please propose query changes at nvim-treesitter or (in this case) the upstream tree-sitter-query project (query and vim parsers are maintained by me so can bundle Neovim queries).",
